        <member name="T:Brega.Loader.Game.GameInputBlock">
            <summary>
            Keeps the game from reacting to input while the Brega menu (or a Brega message box) is shown:
            - the global FsmBool PlayerInMenu is held true (the game's "Update Cursor" FSM then stops mouse-look and frees the
              cursor, the same way the game's own menus do) and restored afterwards;
            - in GAME, the "Open Menu" FSM on Systems/OptionsDB (Esc/F1 open the pause menu, it does not check PlayerInMenu)
              is paused, and resumed one frame after the menu closes, so the Esc that closes our menu does not open the pause
              menu;
            - in MainMenu, every collider of the scene is disabled so clicks do not reach the menu buttons behind us.
            </summary>
        </member>
